{
  "_README": [
    "HAND-CHECKED VERDICTS. Nothing writes this file but a person.",
    "",
    "The audit measures what it can. Some things it cannot: whether a page that",
    "returned 200 without a text container was a login wall, or whether a work",
    "the reader denies has text nonetheless ships a machine-generated PDF. Both",
    "were settled by opening the page. This is where that judgment is recorded",
    "so the About page can report it instead of filing every case under 'the",
    "source has no text'.",
    "",
    "Rules, so this cannot rot the way a hand-typed figure does:",
    "  1. A verdict here NARROWS a finding the audit already made. It can never",
    "     add a work the measurement did not flag -- audit.py errors if it does.",
    "  2. If a later fetch contradicts a verdict (text arrives for a work marked",
    "     no_text), the audit FAILS rather than publishing the stale claim.",
    "  3. Every entry carries who checked it and when. An undated verdict is",
    "     indistinguishable from a guess.",
    "",
    "`no_devanagari` records the hand-check of the OTHER finding: works whose",
    "text carries no Devanagari. These are NOT consumed by the audit -- that",
    "finding is measured, and this only records WHICH KIND of non-Devanagari",
    "each one turned out to be, so the reading is not lost and the next person",
    "can see what was looked at rather than redoing it."
  ],

